# AI Workspace

This repository uses a repo-local AI workspace so coding agents share the same
project instructions, workflows, and rules.

## Canonical Files

| Path | Purpose |
|---|---|
| `AGENTS.md` | Repository-wide instructions |
| nested `AGENTS.md` | Directory-specific instructions |
| `.agents/skills/` | Repeatable workflows |
| `.agents/rules/` | Cross-cutting rules |
| `.agents/agents/` | Reusable agent definitions |

## Generated Files

Some tools require generated copies under tool-specific directories such as
`.claude/` or `.cursor/`. Edit the canonical files under `.agents/` unless a
file explicitly says otherwise.

Sync command:

```text
{AI_SYNC_COMMAND}
```

Hook commands, if installed:

```text
{AI_HOOKS_STATUS_COMMAND}
{AI_HOOKS_ENABLE_COMMAND}
{AI_HOOKS_DISABLE_COMMAND}
```

Enabling hooks writes repository-local git config and should be done only after
reviewing the installed `.githooks/` files.

## Safety

Agents must ask before:

- deleting or overwriting files
- committing or pushing
- modifying secrets
- activating hooks
- installing dependencies
- writing to external services
- running application servers when not explicitly allowed

## Build And Test

Use the repository commands documented in `AGENTS.md`.

## Adding Guidance

- Add reusable workflows with the `create-skill` skill.
- Add coding or process rules with the `create-rule` skill.
- Keep always-loaded instructions short.
- Prefer updating existing guidance over adding duplicates.
